{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs GNU C++11 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following GNU C++11 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nAlice and Bob are playing a game with a string of characters, with Alice going first. The string consists n characters, each of which is one of the first k letters of the alphabet. On a player\u2019s turn, they can either arbitrarily permute the characters in the words, or delete exactly one character in the word (if there is at least one character). In addition, their resulting word cannot have appeared before throughout the entire game. The player unable to make a valid move loses the game.Given n,\u2009k,\u2009p, find the number of words with exactly n characters consisting of the first k letters of the alphabet such that Alice will win if both Alice and Bob play optimally. Return this number modulo the prime number p.\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the GNU C++11 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\n#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nconstexpr int MAX_N = 250005;\nint n, k, mod_val, final_ans;\nint h_power[MAX_N], factorial[MAX_N], inv_factorial[MAX_N], dp[27][MAX_N];\n\nint mod_exp(int base, int exp) {\n    int res = 1;\n    base %= mod_val;\n    while (exp) {\n        if (exp & 1) res = (1LL * res * base) % mod_val;\n        base = (1LL * base * base) % mod_val;\n        exp >>= 1;\n    }\n    return res;\n}\n\nint main() {\n    ios_base::sync_with_stdio(false);\n    cin.tie(nullptr);\n    \n    cin >> n >> k >> mod_val;\n    \n    inv_factorial[0] = inv_factorial[1] = factorial[0] = 1;\n    \n    for (int i = 2; i <= n; ++i) {\n        inv_factorial[i] = 1LL * (mod_val - mod_val / i) * inv_factorial[mod_val % i] % mod_val;\n    }\n    \n    for (int step = 1; step <= n; step <<= 1) {\n        for (int idx = step >> 1; idx < step && idx <= n; ++idx) {\n            h_power[idx] = step;\n        }\n    }\n    \n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        factorial[i] = 1LL * factorial[i-1] * i % mod_val;\n        inv_factorial[i] = 1LL * inv_factorial[i-1] * inv_factorial[i] % mod_val;\n    }\n    \n    final_ans = mod_exp(k, n);\n    \n    if (n % 2 == 0) {\n        fill(&dp[0][0], &dp[27][0], 0);\n        dp[0][0] = 1;\n        \n        for (int level = 0; level < 26; ++level) {\n            for (int mask = 0; mask <= n; ++mask) {\n                if (dp[level][mask] && (mask & n) == mask) {\n                    for (int next_mask = mask + h_power[mask]; next_mask <= n; next_mask = (next_mask + 1) | mask) {\n                        if ((next_mask & n) == next_mask) {\n                            dp[level + 1][next_mask] = (dp[level + 1][next_mask] + 1LL * dp[level][mask] * inv_factorial[next_mask - mask] % mod_val) % mod_val;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        \n        int accum = 0;\n        for (int i = 1; i <= 26; ++i) {\n            accum = (accum + 1LL * dp[i][n] * inv_factorial[k - i] % mod_val) % mod_val;\n        }\n        final_ans = (final_ans - 1LL * accum * factorial[n] % mod_val * factorial[k] % mod_val + mod_val) % mod_val;\n    }\n    \n    cout << final_ans << '\\n';\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp"